Exe 6 License Agreement
This License Agreement governs the use of the admin panel software Exe 6 (hereinafter &quot;Software&quot;), developed and owned by Flare Studio (hereinafter &quot;Licensor&quot;). By checking the agreement box, purchasing, downloading, or using the Software, you (hereinafter &quot;Licensee&quot;) agree to be bound by the terms of this Agreement.

1. Grant of License
Licensor grants the Licensee a non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license to:
1.1 Use the Software in their Roblox games and experiences.
1.2. Modify the source code of the Software for personal use.
1.3. Use the Software in multiple games owned by the Licensee.

2. Limitations
Licensee agrees to the following restrictions:

2.1 Code Sharing
Licensee may share portions of the Software&apos;s source code publicly, provided:
The shared code is isolated and does not include any accompanying elements, assets, or other components necessary for the Software to function.
The shared code cannot be used to reconstruct the Software&apos;s functionality.

Notwithstanding the foregoing, the Licensee is strictly prohibited from publishing, leaking, selling, distributing, or sharing any portion of the Software&apos;s source code that has been decrypted, unpacked, or de-obfuscated, whether in whole or in part.

2.2 Redistribution &amp; Resale
Licensee may not share, upload, distribute, resell, or otherwise make the Software or its components available to others, whether modified or unmodified.
This restriction applies to all elements of the Software, except for the isolated portions of source code as described in Section 2.1.

2.3 Security System
The Software includes a security system designed to ensure proper ownership.
The Software will not function if it is not purchased from the Licensor’s official repository or authorized source. Any attempt to bypass this system is strictly prohibited.

3. Acceptance
By checking the agreement box, purchasing, installing, or using the Software, the Licensee acknowledges and agrees to all terms and conditions outlined in this Agreement.

