="TextLabel" referent="RBX25369"><Properties><Font name="FontFace"><Family><url>rbxasset://fonts/families/Inconsolata.json</url></Family><Weight>400</Weight><Style>Normal</Style></Font><string name="LocalizedText">Flare Studio
Exe 6 Privacy Policy

This Privacy Policy governs the collection, use, storage, and protection of information in connection with the admin panel software Exe 6 (hereinafter &quot;Software&quot;), developed and owned by Flare Studio (hereinafter &quot;Licensor&quot;). Any individual who purchases, downloads, installs, accesses, or uses the Software shall be referred to as the &quot;Licensee&quot;.

1. Information Collected
The Licensor is committed to collecting only the information reasonably necessary to operate, license, and protect the Software.
The Software is designed to minimize the information collected from the Licensee. The information described below constitutes the information collected directly by the Software for the purposes described in this Privacy Policy.

1.1 Roblox Account User ID
When the Licensee selects the &quot;Proceed&quot; button on the License Agreement screen, the Software collects the Licensee&apos;s Roblox Account User ID.

The User ID is collected for the purpose of maintaining a record of the Licensee&apos;s acknowledgment of the Exe 6 License Agreement.
The User ID may also be used where reasonably necessary for the operation, verification, and protection of the Software&apos;s licensing and security systems.
The User ID is encrypted before being stored by the Licensor.

1.2 Action Timestamp
When the Licensee selects the &quot;Proceed&quot; button on the License Agreement screen, the Software records the time at which the action occurred.
The recorded time is stored as a Unix timestamp.
The timestamp is used to maintain an accurate record of the Licensee&apos;s acknowledgment of the Exe 6 License Agreement and relevant licensing or security events.
The timestamp is encrypted before being stored by the Licensor.

2. Use of Collected Information
The Licensor uses the information collected by the Software only for purposes relating to the operation, licensing, security, and administration of the Software.

2.1 License Agreement Acknowledgment
The Roblox Account User ID and associated timestamp are used to maintain a record that the Licensee acknowledged the Exe 6 License Agreement.
Such record may be used to establish which Roblox account performed the acknowledgment and when the acknowledgment occurred.

2.2 Licensing and Security
The information described in Section 1 may be used where reasonably necessary to operate, verify, maintain, and protect the Software&apos;s licensing and security systems.
This includes the prevention and investigation of unauthorized use, abuse, attempts to circumvent licensing protections, or other activity that may compromise the Software or its licensing infrastructure.

2.3 Security Records
The Licensor may use action timestamps to maintain an accurate chronological record of relevant licensing and security events.

3. Anonymous Telemetry
The Software collects a limited amount of anonymous telemetry relating solely to the distribution of the Software.

3.1 Download Count
Each download of the Software contributes +1 to an overall download count.
The resulting count is maintained as an aggregate statistic used to determine how many times the Software has been downloaded.

3.2 Anonymous Information
The telemetry described in this Section is not associated with the Licensee&apos;s Roblox Account User ID, action timestamp, or other personal information.
The telemetry does not identify individual Licensees and is not used to track individual Licensees.

3.3 Purpose of Telemetry
The telemetry is used solely to provide the Licensor with an aggregate measure of Software downloads.
The resulting download count may be displayed to Licensees on the installation page of the Software&apos;s onboarding process.

4. Information Not Collected
The Licensor does not intentionally collect information from the Licensee through the Software that is not reasonably necessary for the purposes described in this Privacy Policy.
The Software does not require the Licensor to collect the Licensee&apos;s:

4.1 Email address
4.2 Geographical region
4.3 Friends
4.4 Membership status
4.5 Game data

The Licensor does not collect information through the Software for advertising or behavioral profiling purposes.

5. Data Storage and Protection
The Licensor takes reasonable measures to protect information collected through the Software against unauthorized access, disclosure, alteration, or destruction.

5.1 Encryption
The Roblox Account User ID and action timestamp collected through the License Agreement screen are encrypted before being stored by the Licensor.

5.2 Access to Information
Access to stored information is limited to the Licensor and systems that reasonably require access for the operation, maintenance, licensing, or security of the Software.

5.3 Security Limitations
Although the Licensor takes reasonable measures to protect stored information, no method of electronic storage or transmission can be guaranteed to be completely secure.

6. Data Retention
The Licensor retains information only for as long as reasonably necessary for the purposes described in this Privacy Policy.

6.1 License Agreement Acknowledgment Records
When the Licensee selects the &quot;Proceed&quot; button on the Exe 6 License Agreement screen, the Software records the action using two pieces of information:

6.1.1 The Licensee&apos;s Roblox Account User ID; and
6.1.2 The Unix timestamp corresponding to the time at which the &quot;Proceed&quot; action occurred.
This record is maintained solely as a record of the Licensee&apos;s acknowledgment of the Exe 6 License Agreement.
The record is not used to establish or provide ownership of the Software. Software ownership and licensing are handled through the Licensor&apos;s authorized distribution and licensing provider.
The User ID and associated timestamp are encrypted before being stored by the Licensor.

These records may be retained for as long as reasonably necessary to maintain an accurate record of License Agreement acknowledgments and to establish, exercise, or defend the Licensor&apos;s legal rights.

6.2 Anonymous Telemetry
Anonymous aggregate download statistics do not contain information identifying individual Licensees.
Each download contributes +1 to an overall download count, which may be retained as statistical information for the purposes described in Section 3.

7. Data Disclosure
The Licensor does not sell the Licensee&apos;s information.

7.1 Advertising
The Licensor does not use information collected through the Software for advertising purposes.

7.2 Behavioral Profiling
The Licensor does not use information collected through the Software to create behavioral profiles of individual Licensees.

7.3 Legal and Security Requirements
The Licensor may disclose information where reasonably necessary to comply with applicable law, respond to a valid legal request, protect the Software or its Licensees, prevent fraud or abuse, or establish, exercise, or defend legal rights.

8. Third-Party Services
The Software uses third-party services to provide certain software distribution and licensing infrastructure.

8.1 Parcel
The Software is distributed through Parcel eCommerce Limited (hereinafter &quot;Parcel&quot;).
Parcel provides software distribution and licensing infrastructure used in connection with the Software.
Information associated with an Exe 6 license may be processed by Parcel where necessary for the provision of its services.
Parcel operates independently from the Licensor and maintains its own privacy practices.
Information processed directly by Parcel is subject to Parcel&apos;s Privacy Policy.

Parcel&apos;s Privacy Policy may be accessed at: https://parcelroblox.com/legal/privacy-policy

8.2 Third-Party Policies
The Licensor does not control the privacy practices of independent third-party service providers.

The Licensee is responsible for reviewing the applicable privacy policies of third-party services used in connection with the Software.

9. Privacy and Data Minimization
The Licensor follows the principle that information should not be collected merely because it can be collected.

9.1 Data Minimization
The Licensor collects only information reasonably necessary for the operation, licensing, and protection of the Software.

9.2 Transparency
The Licensor aims to clearly explain what information is collected, why it is collected, and how it is used.

9.3 No Sale of Information
The Licensor does not sell information collected through the Software.

9.4 No Unnecessary Collection
The Licensor does not intentionally collect information through the Software that is unrelated to the purposes described in this Privacy Policy.

10. Changes to This Privacy Policy
The Licensor may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes to the Software, its services, privacy practices, or applicable legal requirements.

11. Obfuscated Systems
Certain components of the Software are obfuscated to protect its licensing, security, and ownership verification mechanisms from unauthorized modification, tampering, or circumvention.

11.1 LLC Script
The LLC Script is an obfuscated component responsible for ownership verification, installation, uninstallation, download telemetry, and Exe 6 Onboarding Plugin setup.
The LLC Script communicates with the Parcel Whitelist API to perform ownership verification.

11.2 LLC Serial
The LLC Script generates an encrypted LLC Serial containing information specific to the Licensee&apos;s game environment. The LLC Serial is stored within the game&apos;s Workspace attributes and is not transmitted to or shared with the Licensor.

11.3 Manager Script
The Manager Script runs the LLC system within the Licensee&apos;s game and performs licensing and ownership verification through the Parcel Whitelist API.

The Manager Script also controls the distribution of Exe 6 to authorized Team members and is designed to prevent unauthorized users from triggering the distribution process or obtaining access to the Software without proper authorization.

11.4 Purpose of Obfuscation
The LLC Script and Manager Script are obfuscated to protect their security and ownership verification mechanisms from unauthorized inspection, modification, circumvention, or abuse.


Flare Studio
Exe 6

Privacy Policy
Updated September 3, 2026</string><bool name="RichText">true</bool><string name="Text">Flare Studio
Exe 6 Privacy Policy

This Privacy Policy governs the collection, use, storage, and protection of information in connection with the admin panel software Exe 6 (hereinafter &quot;Software&quot;), developed and owned by Flare Studio (hereinafter &quot;Licensor&quot;). Any individual who purchases, downloads, installs, accesses, or uses the Software shall be referred to as the &quot;Licensee&quot;.

1. Information Collected
The Licensor is committed to collecting only the information reasonably necessary to operate, license, and protect the Software.
The Software is designed to minimize the information collected from the Licensee. The information described below constitutes the information collected directly by the Software for the purposes described in this Privacy Policy.

1.1 Roblox Account User ID
When the Licensee selects the &quot;Proceed&quot; button on the License Agreement screen, the Software collects the Licensee&apos;s Roblox Account User ID.

The User ID is collected for the purpose of maintaining a record of the Licensee&apos;s acknowledgment of the Exe 6 License Agreement.
The User ID may also be used where reasonably necessary for the operation, verification, and protection of the Software&apos;s licensing and security systems.
The User ID is encrypted before being stored by the Licensor.

1.2 Action Timestamp
When the Licensee selects the &quot;Proceed&quot; button on the License Agreement screen, the Software records the time at which the action occurred.
The recorded time is stored as a Unix timestamp.
The timestamp is used to maintain an accurate record of the Licensee&apos;s acknowledgment of the Exe 6 License Agreement and relevant licensing or security events.
The timestamp is encrypted before being stored by the Licensor.

2. Use of Collected Information
The Licensor uses the information collected by the Software only for purposes relating to the operation, licensing, security, and administration of the Software.

2.1 License Agreement Acknowledgment
The Roblox Account User ID and associated timestamp are used to maintain a record that the Licensee acknowledged the Exe 6 License Agreement.
Such record may be used to establish which Roblox account performed the acknowledgment and when the acknowledgment occurred.

2.2 Licensing and Security
The information described in Section 1 may be used where reasonably necessary to operate, verify, maintain, and protect the Software&apos;s licensing and security systems.
This includes the prevention and investigation of unauthorized use, abuse, attempts to circumvent licensing protections, or other activity that may compromise the Software or its licensing infrastructure.

2.3 Security Records
The Licensor may use action timestamps to maintain an accurate chronological record of relevant licensing and security events.

3. Anonymous Telemetry
The Software collects a limited amount of anonymous telemetry relating solely to the distribution of the Software.

3.1 Download Count
Each download of the Software contributes +1 to an overall download count.
The resulting count is maintained as an aggregate statistic used to determine how many times the Software has been downloaded.

3.2 Anonymous Information
The telemetry described in this Section is not associated with the Licensee&apos;s Roblox Account User ID, action timestamp, or other personal information.
The telemetry does not identify individual Licensees and is not used to track individual Licensees.

3.3 Purpose of Telemetry
The telemetry is used solely to provide the Licensor with an aggregate measure of Software downloads.
The resulting download count may be displayed to Licensees on the installation page of the Software&apos;s onboarding process.

4. Information Not Collected
The Licensor does not intentionally collect information from the Licensee through the Software that is not reasonably necessary for the purposes described in this Privacy Policy.
The Software does not require the Licensor to collect the Licensee&apos;s:

4.1 Email address
4.2 Geographical region
4.3 Friends
4.4 Membership status
4.5 Game data

The Licensor does not collect information through the Software for advertising or behavioral profiling purposes.

5. Data Storage and Protection
The Licensor takes reasonable measures to protect information collected through the Software against unauthorized access, disclosure, alteration, or destruction.

5.1 Encryption
The Roblox Account User ID and action timestamp collected through the License Agreement screen are encrypted before being stored by the Licensor.

5.2 Access to Information
Access to stored information is limited to the Licensor and systems that reasonably require access for the operation, maintenance, licensing, or security of the Software.

5.3 Security Limitations
Although the Licensor takes reasonable measures to protect stored information, no method of electronic storage or transmission can be guaranteed to be completely secure.

6. Data Retention
The Licensor retains information only for as long as reasonably necessary for the purposes described in this Privacy Policy.

6.1 License Agreement Acknowledgment Records
When the Licensee selects the &quot;Proceed&quot; button on the Exe 6 License Agreement screen, the Software records the action using two pieces of information:

6.1.1 The Licensee&apos;s Roblox Account User ID; and
6.1.2 The Unix timestamp corresponding to the time at which the &quot;Proceed&quot; action occurred.
This record is maintained solely as a record of the Licensee&apos;s acknowledgment of the Exe 6 License Agreement.
The record is not used to establish or provide ownership of the Software. Software ownership and licensing are handled through the Licensor&apos;s authorized distribution and licensing provider.
The User ID and associated timestamp are encrypted before being stored by the Licensor.

These records may be retained for as long as reasonably necessary to maintain an accurate record of License Agreement acknowledgments and to establish, exercise, or defend the Licensor&apos;s legal rights.

6.2 Anonymous Telemetry
Anonymous aggregate download statistics do not contain information identifying individual Licensees.
Each download contributes +1 to an overall download count, which may be retained as statistical information for the purposes described in Section 3.

7. Data Disclosure
The Licensor does not sell the Licensee&apos;s information.

7.1 Advertising
The Licensor does not use information collected through the Software for advertising purposes.

7.2 Behavioral Profiling
The Licensor does not use information collected through the Software to create behavioral profiles of individual Licensees.

7.3 Legal and Security Requirements
The Licensor may disclose information where reasonably necessary to comply with applicable law, respond to a valid legal request, protect the Software or its Licensees, prevent fraud or abuse, or establish, exercise, or defend legal rights.

8. Third-Party Services
The Software uses third-party services to provide certain software distribution and licensing infrastructure.

8.1 Parcel
The Software is distributed through Parcel eCommerce Limited (hereinafter &quot;Parcel&quot;).
Parcel provides software distribution and licensing infrastructure used in connection with the Software.
Information associated with an Exe 6 license may be processed by Parcel where necessary for the provision of its services.
Parcel operates independently from the Licensor and maintains its own privacy practices.
Information processed directly by Parcel is subject to Parcel&apos;s Privacy Policy.

Parcel&apos;s Privacy Policy may be accessed at: https://parcelroblox.com/legal/privacy-policy

8.2 Third-Party Policies
The Licensor does not control the privacy practices of independent third-party service providers.

The Licensee is responsible for reviewing the applicable privacy policies of third-party services used in connection with the Software.

9. Privacy and Data Minimization
The Licensor follows the principle that information should not be collected merely because it can be collected.

9.1 Data Minimization
The Licensor collects only information reasonably necessary for the operation, licensing, and protection of the Software.

9.2 Transparency
The Licensor aims to clearly explain what information is collected, why it is collected, and how it is used.

9.3 No Sale of Information
The Licensor does not sell information collected through the Software.

9.4 No Unnecessary Collection
The Licensor does not intentionally collect information through the Software that is unrelated to the purposes described in this Privacy Policy.

10. Changes to This Privacy Policy
The Licensor may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes to the Software, its services, privacy practices, or applicable legal requirements.

11. Obfuscated Systems
Certain components of the Software are obfuscated to protect its licensing, security, and ownership verification mechanisms from unauthorized modification, tampering, or circumvention.

11.1 LLC Script
The LLC Script is an obfuscated component responsible for ownership verification, installation, uninstallation, download telemetry, and Exe 6 Onboarding Plugin setup.
The LLC Script communicates with the Parcel Whitelist API to perform ownership verification.

11.2 LLC Serial
The LLC Script generates an encrypted LLC Serial containing information specific to the Licensee&apos;s game environment. The LLC Serial is stored within the game&apos;s Workspace attributes and is not transmitted to or shared with the Licensor.

11.3 Manager Script
The Manager Script runs the LLC system within the Licensee&apos;s game and performs licensing and ownership verification through the Parcel Whitelist API.

The Manager Script also controls the distribution of Exe 6 to authorized Team members and is designed to prevent unauthorized users from triggering the distribution process or obtaining access to the Software without proper authorization.

11.4 Purpose of Obfuscation
The LLC Script and Manager Script are obfuscated to protect their security and ownership verification mechanisms from unauthorized inspection, modification, circumvention, or abuse.


